    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "OFF-TIER CALLS",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "praxen-litellm-pg"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 4
      },
      "description": "DETECTOR. Calls in range that the vendor BILLED at a premium service tier (OpenAI 'priority'/'fast' are one server-side tier, about 2x) on a route that did NOT opt in (convention: opt-in routes carry the suffix '-priority'). Source: the proxy's spend log records the billed tier per call in metadata.cost_breakdown.service_tier, taken from the vendor response. Why it exists: an OpenAI organization can default to priority. A bare request with no service_tier field comes back 'priority' and is billed about 2x, with nothing in the config asking for it. Pin service_tier: \"default\" on every direct entry and keep this at 0. Anything else means a route lost its pin, a wildcard route was called bare, or the vendor default changed. CAVEAT: on models that do not echo a tier (OpenAI pro models) the recorded tier is the REQUESTED one and the price stays standard — check x_vs_standard on the table before treating a count here as money lost.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "praxen-litellm-pg"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "rawSql": "SELECT count(*) AS \"off_tier_calls\"\nFROM \"LiteLLM_SpendLogs\"\nWHERE $__timeFilter(\"startTime\")\n  AND metadata->'cost_breakdown'->>'service_tier' IN ('priority','fast')\n  AND model_group !~ '-priority$'"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#3FA37A",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#D9822B",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "#C8464A",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Billed Service Tier // route - tier - x vs standard rate (range)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "praxen-litellm-pg"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "description": "Per route (model_group) and BILLED tier: calls, tokens, billed $ vs what the same tokens cost at the model's STANDARD rate (recomputed from the price map the proxy recorded on each row: input, output, cache-read and cache-write rates) and the ratio. verdict 'OFF-TIER' = premium tier on a route that did not opt in; 'opt-in lane' = an explicit -priority route (ratio about 2.00); 'discount' = flex; 'standard' = 1.00. The tier string is the trigger; the ratio is informative and drifts where an entry carries an injected price override, where cached tokens dominate, or above a long-context pricing boundary. Anthropic reports 'standard'/'priority'; Gemini, xAI and Perplexity 'default'; local model servers report no tier and are excluded. Only rows carrying cost_breakdown appear (LiteLLM proxy releases from mid-2026). CAVEAT (probe 2026-09-10): the tier string is the tier the proxy RESOLVED — the vendor's echo when present, otherwise the tier that was REQUESTED. OpenAI's pro models return no tier and are priced at standard even when priority was requested, so a 'priority' row at x_vs_standard 1.00 means requested-but-not-applied, not a premium paid.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "praxen-litellm-pg"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "rawSql": "WITH r AS (\n  SELECT\n    model_group,\n    custom_llm_provider AS provider,\n    metadata->'cost_breakdown'->>'service_tier' AS tier,\n    spend,\n    prompt_tokens,\n    completion_tokens,\n    COALESCE((metadata->'usage_object'->'prompt_tokens_details'->>'cached_tokens')::bigint, 0) AS cached_tok,\n    COALESCE((metadata->'usage_object'->'prompt_tokens_details'->>'cache_creation_tokens')::bigint, 0) AS cache_write_tok,\n    (metadata->'model_map_information'->'model_map_value'->>'input_cost_per_token')::float AS in_rate,\n    (metadata->'model_map_information'->'model_map_value'->>'output_cost_per_token')::float AS out_rate,\n    (metadata->'model_map_information'->'model_map_value'->>'cache_read_input_token_cost')::float AS cr_rate,\n    (metadata->'model_map_information'->'model_map_value'->>'cache_creation_input_token_cost')::float AS cw_rate,\n    \"startTime\"\n  FROM \"LiteLLM_SpendLogs\"\n  WHERE $__timeFilter(\"startTime\")\n    AND metadata->'cost_breakdown'->>'service_tier' IS NOT NULL\n),\nx AS (\n  SELECT *,\n    CASE WHEN in_rate IS NOT NULL AND out_rate IS NOT NULL THEN\n      GREATEST(prompt_tokens - cached_tok - cache_write_tok, 0) * in_rate\n      + cached_tok * COALESCE(cr_rate, in_rate)\n      + cache_write_tok * COALESCE(cw_rate, in_rate)\n      + completion_tokens * out_rate\n    END AS std_usd\n  FROM r\n)\nSELECT\n  model_group AS \"route\",\n  provider,\n  tier,\n  CASE WHEN tier IN ('priority','fast') AND model_group !~ '-priority$' THEN 'OFF-TIER ⚠'\n       WHEN tier IN ('priority','fast') THEN 'opt-in lane'\n       WHEN tier = 'flex' THEN 'discount'\n       ELSE 'standard' END AS \"verdict\",\n  count(*) AS \"calls\",\n  sum(prompt_tokens) AS \"in_tok\",\n  sum(completion_tokens) AS \"out_tok\",\n  round(sum(spend)::numeric, 5) AS \"billed_usd\",\n  round(sum(std_usd)::numeric, 5) AS \"std_rate_usd\",\n  round((sum(spend) / NULLIF(sum(std_usd), 0))::numeric, 2) AS \"x_vs_standard\",\n  max(\"startTime\") AS \"last_seen\"\nFROM x\nGROUP BY model_group, provider, tier\nORDER BY (tier IN ('priority','fast') AND model_group !~ '-priority$') DESC, \"x_vs_standard\" DESC NULLS LAST, sum(spend) DESC"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "billed_usd"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "currencyUSD"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "std_rate_usd"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "currencyUSD"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "x_vs_standard"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "basic"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "thresholds",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "absolute",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "color": "#3F7FA3",
                      "value": null
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "#3FA37A",
                      "value": 0.95
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "#D9822B",
                      "value": 1.15
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "#C8464A",
                      "value": 1.6
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "verdict"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "OFF-TIER ⚠": {
                        "color": "#C8464A",
                        "index": 0
                      },
                      "opt-in lane": {
                        "color": "#3F7FA3",
                        "index": 1
                      },
                      "discount": {
                        "color": "#3FA37A",
                        "index": 2
                      },
                      "standard": {
                        "color": "#6B7A88",
                        "index": 3
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-text"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "last_seen"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "dateTimeAsIso"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": {
          "show": false,
          "reducer": [
            "sum"
          ],
          "countRows": false
        },
        "sortBy": []
      }
    },
